lse diff --quiet HEAD -- $DMR` exits 0.\n129: \n130: ### Wave 2, lane WG8: install guide and embedder host\n131: - [x] T038 Name the accepted runtimes instead of a count (`DIP`, `DIY`, `DICT`). Test first: in `DICT`, add a case asserting `DIP` holds no `outside the seven`, names `claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin and pi or the ones already there` and says DSH is not offered, and that `DIY`'s `runtimes` input says DSH is not offered. Then change `A runtime name outside the seven` in `DIP` to `A runtime name outside claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin and pi or the ones already there`, add `DSH is not offered, because the link manifest has no DSH row.` after that paragraph and append ` DSH is not offered, because the link manifest has no dsh row.` to the `runtimes` input of `DIY`. Verify: before the change the case fails, after it `NT $DICT` reports `fail 0`.\n132: - [x] T039 Bind the embedder's start and pull to the resolved host (`DEM`, `SARC`). Test first: in `SARC`, add a case asserting the start and pull steps of `DEM` name `OLLAMA_HOST` taken from the resolved URL and that a URL whose host is not `127.0.0.1`, `localhost` or `::1` is refused before either runs. Then change the start step to run `OLLAMA_HOST=<host:port of the resolved URL> ollama serve` and the pull step to run `OLLAMA_HOST=<host:port of the resolved URL> ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, and add before them `When the resolved URL's host is not 127.0.0.1, localhost or ::1, start and pull nothing. That server is the operator's, so end with STATUS=FAIL naming the URL and the install guide's start and pull commands.` Verify: before the change the case fails, after it `NT $SARC` reports `fail 0`.\n133: \n134: ### Wave 2, lane WG9: holdout rows out of the published baseline\n135: - [ ] T040 Publish no per-row outcome for a holdout row (`CAP`, `SLT`). Test first: in `SLT`, add `it('publishes no holdout row', ...)` expecting no key of `baseline.rows`, `baseline.attachedMetrics.attachedRows` or `baseline.attachedMetrics.typedRows` to be a corpus id whose `split` is `holdout`, and filter the id list of the row-by-row comparison to non-holdout corpus ids. Then in `CAP`, write `rows[row.id]`, `attachedRows[row.id]` and `typedRowResults[row.id]` only when `row.split !== 'holdout'`, leave every tally as it is and add a comment saying a holdout row's outcome is what the split exists to keep unseen, so only its counts are published. Verify: `VX tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` reports exactly 1 failed, the new case naming 44 ids, which T041 clears, `node --check $CAP` exits 0, `node $CAP | jq -c '.rows | length'` prints 132 and `FLOOR` prints its lines in `$SP/before.txt`.\n136: - [ ] T041 Recapture the baseline without holdout rows (`BASE`). Run after T013 and T040. First set `PREV=\"$(mktemp)\"` and run `node $CAP > \"$PREV\"`, then `diff <(jq -S '{metrics, commands, attachedMetrics: (.attachedMetrics | del(.attachedRows, .typedRows))}' \"$PREV\") <(jq -S '{metrics, commands, attachedMetrics: (.attachedMetrics | del(.attachedRows, .typedRows))}' $BASE) > $SP/baseline-delta.txt`, then `node $CAP --write` and remove `PREV`. Verify: `HOLD` prints `{\"holdout\":44,\"rows\":0,\"attachedRows\":0,\"typedRows\":0}`, `VX tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `FLOOR` prints lines equal to or better than `$SP/before.txt` and `$SP/baseline-delta.txt` is empty or names only holdout aggregates under `attachedMetrics`.\n137: \n138: ### Wave 2, lane WG11: session readers\n139: - [x] T042 Fall back to the Devin transcript when the database fails (`$SR/devin.mjs`, `$SRT/devin.test.mjs`). Test first: in the test file, add a case that builds `devinSession({ root, projectDir })`, overwrites `fixture.dbPath` with `not a database` and expects `readSession` to return `ok` with `source.locatorKind` `transcript_file` and first item text `Read the file.`. Today it returns `store_unreadable`. Then in `loadDevinSession`, on an open failure, a `null` projection or a thrown query, return the result of `loadTranscript(sessionId, dataDirectory, options)` when it is `ok` or a `session_mismatch`, and `store_unreadable` otherwise. Keep the `working_directory` mismatch as it is. Add a comment saying a damaged or older database must not hide a transcript the store still holds, while a transcript that also fails keeps the store unreadable. Verify: before the change the case fails, after it `NT $SRT/devin.test.mjs` reports `fail 0`.\n140: - [x] T043 Pin the sourceless DSH message rule (`$SRT/dsh.test.mjs`). Add a case: a DSH fixture with an appended `user/message` event whose `data` has no `source` and whose content is `[{ type: 'text', text: 'notice' }]` loads with `injected` holding `{ source: 'unknown', text: 'notice' }` and no record carrying `notice`. It passes today and pins the fail-closed rule the readers README states. Verify: `NT $SRT/dsh.test.mjs` reports `fail 0` with one more test than before.\n141: - [x] T044 Add the readers' runtime table to the parity test (`PAR`). Add an `it` that imports `capabilities` from `../../../../../hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs` and expects `Object.keys(capabilities).sort()` to equal `[...ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES].sort()`, with a comment saying the readers' table is a fourth hand-spelled runtime list. It passes today and fails the day one list gains a runtime alone. Verify: `VX tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed with one more case than before.\n142: - [x] T045 Read the path the containment check resolved (`$SR/claude.mjs`, `$SR/devin.mjs`, `$SR/dsh.mjs`, `$SR/pi.mjs`). In `claude.mjs` and in `loadTranscript` of `devin.mjs`, read `storePath` instead of `transcriptPath`. In `dsh.mjs`, read `storePath` instead of `logPath` and keep `logPath` as the decoder's name argument. In `pi.mjs`, read `guard.path` instead of `filePath`. Add one comment in each saying the file read is the one the containment check resolved, so a path swapped after the check is not followed. Verify: `VSR` reports `fail 0` and `rg -n \"readFileSync\\((transcriptPath|logPath|filePath)\" $SR/claude.mjs $SR/devin.mjs $SR/dsh.mjs $SR/pi.mjs` prints nothing.\n143: - [x] T046 Describe the fallback, the sourceless rule and the contained read (`SRR`). In the code table, change the Devin `store_unreadable` row to say an open or projection failure falls back to the transcript first. Add a sentence that a DSH `user/message` with no source is kept as injected with source `unknown` and never as a record, and one that each reader opens the path its containment check resolved. Verify: `rg -c \"falls back to the transcript\" $SRR` prints 1, `rg -c \"with no source\" $SRR` prints 1 and `rg -c \"containment check resolved\" $SRR` prints 1.\n144: - [x] T047 Regenerate the reader declarations (`$SR/*.d.mts`, `$SR/*.d.mts.map`). Run `SRD` and do not edit a declaration by hand. Verify: `SRD --check` prints `current`, `VSR` reports `fail 0` and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- $SR` lists only `.mjs`, `.d.mts`, `.d.mts.map` and `README.md` files.\n145: \n146: ### Wave 2, lane WG12: subprocess output cap and bench matrix\n147: - [x] T048 Cap the advisor child's stdout and stderr (`SUB`, `SUBT`). Test first: create `SUBT` with a case that writes a temporary script printing `JSON.stringify(['x'.repeat(2 * 1024 * 1024)])` and calls `runAdvisorSubprocess('prompt', { workspaceRoot: <temp>, pythonBin: process.execPath, scriptPath: <script>, timeoutMs: 10000 })`, expecting `errorCode` `JSON_PARSE_FAILED`, and a case whose script writes 2 MiB to stderr and exits 1, expecting `(result.stderr ?? '').length` at most `1024 * 1024`. Today the first reads another code because the whole array arrives. Then add `MAX_OUTPUT_CHARS = 1024 * 1024` and a `capOutput(current, chunk)` shaped like `capStdout` in `hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`, and use it in both `data` handlers of `runSpawnAttempt`, with a comment saying only the timeout bounded the child's output before, so a runaway child could hold the hook's memory until it was killed. Verify: before the change the first case fails, after it `VX tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n148: - [x] T049 Give every advisor runtime a bench matrix row (`BENCH`). Add rows for `pi`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin` and `dsh` to `SEVEN_AXIS_MATRIX` with `not-recorded` on each of the seven axes, change the header line naming `claude/opencode` to say the iteration measured Claude and OpenCode and the rest read `not-recorded`, and add a comment saying an invented axis reading would pass for a measured one. Verify: before the change `VB` reports `1 failed | 3 passed (4)`, after it `VB` reports `4 passed (4)`.\n149: \n150: ### Wave 2, lane WG13: advisor docs against code\n151: - [x] T050 Say 46 command rows (`AR`, `CMM`). Change `the 45 command rows` in `AR` and `45 rows in all` in `CMM` to 46. Verify: `rg -c \"45 (command )?rows|45 rows in all\" $AR $CMM` prints nothing and `node $DER --check | jq .counts.typescriptActive` prints 46.\n152: - [x] T051 Name the DSH prompt adapter (`ARCH`). In the adapter sentence, change `for Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin and Pi` to `for Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, DSH and Pi` and add that the DSH adapter, `hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, runs the Claude handler from `runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`. Verify: `rg -c \"hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs\" $ARCH` prints 1 and `rg -c \"Devin, DSH and Pi\" $ARCH` prints 1.\n153: - [x] T052 Give the row shape, the policy source and the gates as the code applies them (`ARM`). In the contract paragraph, give the row shape as `{ command, policy?, mutating?, ownerSkillId }`, say `mutating` is the class the renderer's child downgrade reads and replace the `COMMAND_POLICIES[command]` sentence with one saying the attached command takes its policy from `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy`, the table keyed by runnable string that covers every tracked command. In the attach paragraph, replace the `system-deep-loop` sentence with one saying the prompt must type the same command or hold a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase, and add that a prompt matching `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command from any hub. Verify: `rg -c \"COMMAND_POLICIES\" $ARM` prints nothing, `rg -c \"mutating\\?\" $ARM` prints 1, `rg -c \"TRACKED_COMMANDS\\[command\\]\\.policy\" $ARM` prints 1 and `rg -c \"NO_EDIT_REQUEST\" $ARM` prints 1.\n154: \n155: ### Wave 3, lane WG10: routing-accuracy README\n156: - [ ] T053 Count and list every file in the folder (`RA`). Set `Code files` to 14 and add one row to the file table for each of `build-holdout.mjs`, `capture-local-native-divergence-ledger.mjs`, `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs`, `derive-ambiguity-slice.mjs`, `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, `reject-unknown-options.mjs`, `score-outcome-rerank.mjs`, `worktree-restore.mjs`, `ambiguity-prompts.jsonl`, `doctor-prompts.jsonl`, `holdout-prompts.jsonl`, `labeled-prompts.jsonl` and `scorer-eval-baseline.json`, each described from its header comment or, for a data file, from its fields and the script that reads it. Describe `holdout-prompts.jsonl` from `rg -l holdout-prompts $RAD` only and never open it. Verify: `rg -c \"^\\| Code files \\| 14 \\|\" $RA` prints 1 and ``rg -c '^\\| `[^`]+\\.(mjs|py|jsonl|json)` \\|' $RA`` prints 21.\n157: - [ ] T054 Describe exit 3, the arena refusal and the allowlisted environment in the runner row (`RA`). Say exit 3 (`head_moved`) ends the arm without the restore, because a commit or a stash made during the turn is not the runner's to discard, add `arena_unprepared` to the exit 2 refusals and add that a live turn gets only the allowlisted environment, the shell basics and each runtime's own prefixes plus the GitHub and git overrides. Verify: `rg -c \"head_moved\" $RA` prints at least 1, `rg -c \"arena_unprepared\" $RA` prints 1 and `rg -c \"allowlist\" $RA` prints at least 1.\n158: - [ ] T055 Say what `offerReached` counts and that the baseline publishes no holdout row (`RA`). In the scorer row, replace `offerReached counts offers on a turn whose brief arrived` with `offerReached counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so a row whose brief state is unknown counts`. In the capture row, add that its `rows`, `attachedRows` and `typedRows` maps leave out every holdout row and only holdout counts are published. Verify: `rg -c \"whose brief arrived\" $RA` prints nothing, `rg -c \"not shown missing\" $RA` prints 1 and `rg -c \"leave out every holdout row\" $RA` prints 1.\n159: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n160: \n161: ---\n162: \n163: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n164: ## Phase 3: Verification\n165: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 166]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md, lines 1-165\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 14: review-remediation\"\n3: description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that fix review pass one's work groups WG1 to WG13: the embed write safety, the attach-path guards, the renderer contract, the runner containment and the advisory fixes in checks, workflows, the baseline, readers, the subprocess, the bench and docs, each with a failing-then-passing test where one can exist.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"review remediation tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 14: review-remediation\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: | `[C]` | Coordinator task: a gate, a full-suite run, an arena build or the close-out. No worker runs it |\n26: \n27: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n28: \n29: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise. Each short name below is defined once.\n30: - `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `VX <file>` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run <file>` in `ADV`. `VALL` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run` in `ADV`, which must report 0 failed.\n31: - `DS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts` and `DA` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets`. `NT <file>` is `node --test <file>`. `DALL` is `node --test $DS/tests/*.test.cjs`, which must report `fail 0`.\n32: - WG1: `EMB` is `$DS/agents-md-embed.cjs` and `EMBT` is `$DS/tests/agents-md-embed.test.cjs`. `DAE` is `$DA/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml`, `DAP` is `$DA/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt` and `DAC` is `$DS/tests/doctor-agents-md-contract.test.cjs`.\n33: - WG2: `CA` is `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` and `CAG` is `$ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` (new). `FU` is `$ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`. `DER` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs` and `DERIVE` is `node $DER --check | jq -r .status`, which must print `fresh`. `CBR` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md` and `LR` is `$ADV/lib/README.md`. `SINGLE(m)` in a test is `{ action: 'route', selectionKind: 'single', targets: [{ workflowMode: m }] }`.\n34: - WG3: `RD` is `$ADV/lib/render.ts`. `GT` is `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts`, `ENV` is `$ADV/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` and `RCS` is `$ADV/tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts`.\n35: - WG4: `RAD` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy`. `R` is `$RAD/run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `ARB` is `$RAD/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, `S` is `$RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs` and `BG` is `$ADV/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` (new). `MARK` is the file name `skilled-behaviour-arena`. `P7` is `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch`, read-only. `G2SUM` is `node $S --summary $P7/runs-g2.jsonl --json | jq -cS 'map_values(.g2.startRate)'`, which printed `{\"claude\":\"3 of 6\",\"codex\":\"0 of 6\",\"devin\":\"4 of 6\",\"dsh\":\"3 of 4\",\"opencode\":\"5 of 6\",\"pi\":\"4 of 6\"}` at planning.\n36: - WG5: `CHK` is `$DS/agents-md-check.cjs`, `CHKT` is `$DS/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs` and `DSR` is `$DS/README.markdown`.\n37: - WG6: `CK` is `$DS/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` and `CKT` its test `$DS/tests/codex-hook-approval-check.test.cjs`. `HW` is `$DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs` and `HWT` its test `$DS/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`.\n38: - WG7: `DSY` is `$DA/doctor-setup.yaml`, `DSM` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md`, `DSP` is `$DA/doctor-setup-presentation.txt`, `DSC` is `$DA/doctor-symlink-check.yaml`, `DMR` is `$DA/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml` and `DSCT` is `$DS/tests/doctor-setup-contract.test.cjs` (new).\n39: - WG8: `DIP` is `$DA/doctor-install-presentation.txt`, `DIY` is `$DA/doctor-install.yaml` and `DICT` is `$DS/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs`. `DEM` is `$DA/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` and `SARC` is `$DS/tests/skill-advisor-route-contract.test.cjs`.\n40: - WG9: `CAP` is `$RAD/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, `BASE` is `$RAD/command-routing-baseline.json`, `CORPUS` is `$RAD/command-prompts.jsonl` and `SLT` is `$ADV/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`. `HOLD` is the holdout id count in `spec.md` section 2, the `jq -n --slurpfile h ... --slurpfile b $BASE` line, which reads only `id` and `split` from `CORPUS`.\n41: - WG10: `RA` is `$RAD/README.md`.\n42: - WG11: `SR` is `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers` and `SRT` is `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers`. `VSR` is `node --test $SRT/*.test.mjs`, which must report `fail 0`. `SRD` is `node .skilled/hooks/shared/session-reader-declarations.mjs`, and `SRD --check` must print a line containing `current`. `SRR` is `$SR/README.md` and `PAR` is `$ADV/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`.\n43: - WG12: `SUB` is `$ADV/lib/subprocess.ts` and `SUBT` is `$ADV/tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` (new). `BENCH` is `$ADV/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` and `VB` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD SPECKIT_RUN_BENCHES=true npx vitest run bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` in `ADV`.\n44: - WG13: `SKA` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor`. `AR` is `$SKA/README.md`, `ARCH` is `$SKA/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CMM` is `$SKA/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md` and `ARM` is `$SKA/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`.\n45: - `FLOOR` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.typed, .attachedMetrics.plain.tune'`, which printed `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}` and `{\"own\":8,\"attached\":15,\"combined\":23,\"total\":45}` at planning. `EVAL` is `node $RAD/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`, which printed `[160,50,21,5]`. `RV` is `bash $DS/route-validate.sh` and `SRM` is `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`, both of which must exit 0.\n46: - `SP` is this phase's `scratch/` folder and `PL` is `$SP/planning`, which holds the six probes spec section 2 ran. Each probe's first comment line says how to run it.\n47: \n48: Rules for every task:\n49: - Each task is one change to the files it names. A task that names a module and its test writes the test case first, runs it and sees it fail for the reason the task names, then makes the change and sees it pass. Its verify names both runs.\n50: - No task reads or prints the prompt text of a row whose `split` is `holdout`. Count holdout rows by `id` and `split` only, and never open `holdout-prompts.jsonl`.\n51: - No worker starts a model session (`claude`, `codex`, `opencode`, `pi`, `devin`, `dsh`), runs a live arm, approves a Codex hook or writes under the home folder. A test builds its trees under a temporary folder and removes them.\n52: - No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id, a finding id, an ADR or a REQ id. State the durable reason instead. T060 checks it.\n53: - Do not edit `AGENTS.md`, the parent `spec.md`, another phase, any `package.json`, `$ADV/lib/scorer/text.ts` or any routing input. Add no dependency.\n54: - A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write.\n55: - Run Vitest with `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD` unless a task says otherwise, because a dispatched worker inherits `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`.\n56: - When a verify prints something other than the expected output, do not change code to match it. Mark the task `[B]` with the printed line.\n57: \n58: Worker lanes. A lane is one worker running its tasks in the order listed. Lanes in one wave own different files and run in parallel. Each task owns the files in its parentheses.\n59: - Wave 0, one worker: T001, T002. Read-only for the repository.\n60: - Gate: T003 [C].\n61: - Wave 1, the safety lane. WG1: T004, T005, T006, T007, T008. WG2: T009, T010, T011, T012, T013, T014. WG3: T015, T016, T017, T018. WG4: T019, T020, T021, T022, T023.\n62: - Wave 2, the advisory lane, after every wave 1 lane ends. WG5: T024, T025, T026, T027, T028. WG6: T029, T030, T031. WG7: T032, T033, T034, T035, T036, T037. WG8: T038, T039. WG9: T040, T041. WG11: T042, T043, T044, T045, T046, T047. WG12: T048, T049. WG13: T050, T051, T052.\n63: - Wave 3, after every wave 2 lane ends. WG10: T053, T054, T055.\n64: - Verification, one at a time: T056, T057, T058, T059, T060, T061, all [C].\n65: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n66: \n67: ---\n68: \n69: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n70: ## Phase 1: Setup\n71: \n72: - [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `VALL`, `DALL`, `VSR`, `SRD --check`, `DERIVE`, `RV`, `SRM`, `G2SUM`, `HOLD` and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false rev-parse --short HEAD`, and write each command with its last output lines or its exit code into `before.txt`. When a gate is red here, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because a red before number cannot be held. Verify: `FLOOR` and `EVAL` print the planning lines in Task Notation, `TC`, `RV` and `SRM` exit 0, `VALL` reports 0 failed, `DALL` and `VSR` report `fail 0`, `SRD --check` prints `current`, `DERIVE` prints `fresh`, `G2SUM` prints its planning line, `HOLD` prints `{\"holdout\":44,\"rows\":44,\"attachedRows\":0,\"typedRows\":0}` and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 13.\n73: - [x] T002 Record the reproductions (`$SP/repro-before.txt`). Run the six probes in `PL`, then `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 npx vitest run tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` in `ADV` and `VB`, and append each command and its output to `repro-before.txt`. Verify: `rg -c \"main threw: EACCES|target .cursor/rules/repo-local.md: replace|10 failed \\| 5 passed \\(15\\)|1 failed \\| 3 passed \\(4\\)|/create:agent \\(start\\)\" $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 5.\n74: - [x] T003 [C] Record the order against phase 015 (`$SP/before.txt`). Read phase 015's `tasks.md` and the worktree status, and append one line starting `order:` that names each spec section 3 file a phase 015 task also edits and which phase builds it first. No wave 1 task starts before this line exists. Verify: `rg -c \"^order:\" $SP/before.txt` prints 1.\n75: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n76: \n77: ---\n78: \n79: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n80: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n81: \n82: ### Wave 1, lane WG1: embed write safety\n83: - [x] T004 Verify every backup entry before restoring any (`EMB`, `EMBT`). Test first: in `EMBT`, add a case on the `foreign` fixture whose write hook, on its first call, overwrites the `AGENTS.md` copy inside the backup folder the plan printed with other bytes and then writes the root document with one shipped line removed, as `dropALineOnWrite` does. Today the post-write proof restores the damaged copy without a word. Then make `restoreFromBackup` walk `record.paths` first, run `assertWritable(root, entry.path)` on each and compare `sha256` of each existing entry's backup copy with `entry.sha256`, and on the first failure print `ERROR: the backup copy of <path> does not match its recorded hash, so nothing was restored. The backup is kept at <dir>` and return `null` before any write. Only then copy and return the count as today. In the drop branch of `commandApply`, print `the write dropped <n> line(s) and the backup could not be restored, so the tree is as the write left it` when the restore returns `null`. Verify: before the change `NT $EMBT` reports 1 failed on the new case and after it reports `fail 0`, with the case asserting the ERROR line and that `AGENTS.md` does not hold the damaged bytes.\n84: - [x] T005 Undo a write that throws mid-apply and exit 3 (`EMB`, `EMBT`). Test first: in `EMBT`, add a case on the `claude-only` fixture with `--create-router` whose write hook throws an `EACCES` error on its second call. Record `treeDigest(dir)` before the apply and expect `embed.main` to return 3 and the output to hold `restored:`, `backup:`, `undo:` and `STATUS=FAIL`. `treeDigest(dir)` must then equal the recorded digest. Today `main` throws. Then wrap the write loop in `commandApply` in `try` and `catch`, and on a throw print `ERROR: writing <path> failed: <message>`, call `restoreFromBackup`, print the `backup:` and `undo:` lines, print `STATUS=FAIL` and return 3. Add exit 3 to `USAGE` and to the header's exit-code lines as `3 a write failed after the backup, and the run was undone or the restore said why not`, with a comment saying a partial write is neither nothing written nor a finished run, so it gets its own exit. Verify: before the change the case fails with the thrown `EACCES`, after it `NT $EMBT` reports `fail 0` and `node $PL/probe-embed-write-fault.cjs` prints `main returned 3`, `apply printed backup line: true, undo line: true, restored line: true` and `after: CLAUDE.md`.\n85: - [x] T006 Fail plan and apply on a foreign line (`EMB`, `EMBT`). Test first: in `EMBT`, add a case on the `foreign` fixture whose write hook puts the line `A line no template ships.` at the top of the root document. Expect apply to return 1, to print that line after `foreign:` and `STATUS=FAIL`, and to leave the root document equal to its original bytes. Today it ends `STATUS=OK`. Then in `commandPlan` and in the pre-write proof of `commandApply`, handle a non-empty `checked.foreign` as `checked.dropped` is handled, printing `foreign: <line> (outside the block and not a shipped line)` for each. In the post-write branch, restore when `after.dropped` or `after.foreign` is non-empty and print both lists. Verify: before the change the case fails on `STATUS=OK`, after it `NT $EMBT` reports `fail 0` and `node $PL/probe-postwrite-foreign.cjs | rg -c \"apply exit 0\"` prints 15.\n86: - [x] T007 Refuse a linked router or Cursor mirror the run would write (`EMB`, `EMBT`). Test first: in `EMBT`, add three cases. On the `foreign` fixture, link `.cursor/rules/repo-local.md` to `../../.github/ci.yml` holding `name: ci`: plan exits 2, its stderr names the link and `../../.github/ci.yml` and the CI file is unchanged. Seed the rule corpus with `seedRuleCorpus`, write `partialRouter(2)` to `docs/router.md` and link `REPO RULES.md` to it: plan exits 2. Write the full router, `partialRouter` over every shipped row, to `docs/router.md` instead: plan does not refuse and lists `REPO RULES.md` as `unchanged`. Today the first and second plans exit 0. Then in `compose`, once the router action and the mirror action are decided, throw `PreconditionError` with `<path> is a symlink to <target>, and writing through it would change the file it points at` when `isSymlink` holds for that path and its action is `create`, `replace` or `remove`. Rewrite the comment above the root-document check to name all three paths. Verify: before the change the first two cases fail on exit 0, after it `NT $EMBT` reports `fail 0` and `bash $PL/probe-mirror-link.sh` prints `plan exit=2` and a `ci.yml` line whose before and after digests are equal.\n87: - [x] T008 Read the new exits in the embed workflow and presentation (`DAE`, `DAP`). In `DAE`, add a row after the exit 1 row: `Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup. When the output holds restored:, the engine put every recorded path back: quote the ERROR line, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and say the tree is as the plan found it. When it holds nothing was restored, the tree is as the failed write left it: show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step.` Change the exit 1 row to say the proof found a dropped line or a `foreign:` line, and that the engine restored by itself unless it printed `nothing was restored`. Add `a symlinked REPO RULES.md or Cursor mirror the run would write` to the exit 2 precondition list. In `DAP`, after the sentence about an embed that exits 1, add `An embed that exits 3 had a write fail after its backup. Its Changed: is none when the output holds restored:, and otherwise the reply says the tree is partly written and its Next: is the undo command the engine printed.` Verify: `rg -c \"Exit 3 means\" $DAE` prints 1, `rg -c \"foreign:\" $DAE` prints at least 1, `rg -c \"exits 3\" $DAP` prints 1 and `NT $DAC` reports `fail 0`.\n88: \n89: ### Wave 1, lane WG2: attach-path guards and the dead policy table\n90: - [x] T009 Offer no hub command on a no-edit prompt (`CA`, `CAG`). Test first: create `CAG` with three cases: `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-skill'), 'use sk-doc to create a skill called invoice-parser, do not change anything yet')` returns `undefined`, the same call without `, do not change anything yet` returns `/create:skill` and `NO_EDIT_REQUEST.test('just show me the plan')` is true. Then add `export const NO_EDIT_REQUEST` to `CA` with the pattern `fusion.ts` declares today and its comment, and in `attachCommand`, after the route shape checks, return `undefined` when `NO_EDIT_REQUEST.test(prompt.toLowerCase())`. Add a comment saying a reader who rules out a change gets no command from either path, so the hub route never offers what the scorer already withholds. Leave `FU` to T012. Verify: before the change `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports failures, after it 0 failed, `rg -c \"^import\" $CA` prints nothing and `TC` exits 0.\n91: - [x] T010 Open the deep-loop gate only for the command being attached (`CA`, `CAG`). Test first: in `CAG`, add four cases on `attachCommand('system-deep-loop', SINGLE('review'), <prompt>)`: `what did /deep:ai-council decide` and `what did /deep:reviw decide` return `undefined`, while `run /deep:review now` and `review the parser in depth` return `/deep:review`. Then change the gate so it opens only when `typedCommandIn(prompt)` equals `commands[workflowMode]` or `DEPTH_REQUEST` matches, and rewrite its comment to say typing another deep-loop command asks for that command, not this one. Verify: before the change 2 of the 4 cases fail, after it `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node --experimental-strip-types --no-warnings $PL/probe-attach.mts | sed -n 2,3p` prints `... -> undefined` and `... -> \"/deep:review\"`.\n92: - [x] T011 Stop a file name reading as a typed command (`CA`, `CAG`). Test first: in `CAG`, add cases: `typedCommandIn('see /create:skill.md for details')` and `typedCommandIn('open /create:readme/notes.txt')` return `undefined`, `typedCommandIn('run /create:skill.')`, `typedCommandIn('run /create:skill, then stop')` and `typedCommandIn('/create:skill-parent now')` return `/create:skill`, `/create:skill