ib/scorer/projection.ts $ADV/scripts/skill_advisor.py` prints nothing, because the deriver's other outputs do not change, and `$SP/wg2-slice.txt` reads 0 failed or names only holdout aggregates under `attachedMetrics`, which T041 recaptures.\n95: - [x] T014 Name the guards and the policy table in the two READMEs (`CBR`, `LR`). In `CBR`, delete the sentence that says the block holds `COMMAND_POLICIES` and add that a surface attaching a command reads its policy from `TRACKED_COMMANDS`. In `LR`'s `command-attach.ts` row, replace the sentence about `/deep:` with `A system-deep-loop command needs the same command typed in the prompt or a DEPTH_WORDING phrase, and a prompt that matches NO_EDIT_REQUEST gets no command.` and keep `The module has no imports.` Verify: `rg -c \"COMMAND_POLICIES\" $CBR $LR` prints nothing, `rg -o \"TRACKED_COMMANDS\" $CBR | wc -l` prints at least 2, where it printed 1 before, and `rg -c \"NO_EDIT_REQUEST\" $LR` prints 1.\n96: \n97: ### Wave 1, lane WG3: renderer contract and test isolation\n98: - [x] T015 Isolate the golden and envelope tests from the child marker (`GT`, `ENV`). Test first: run `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 npx vitest run tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` in `ADV` and see `10 failed`. Then in each file import `beforeEach`, `afterEach` and `vi` from `vitest`, and inside each top-level `describe` add `beforeEach(() => { vi.stubEnv('AI_SESSION_CHILD', '') })` and `afterEach(() => { vi.unstubAllEnvs() })`, with a comment saying the expected heads are the interactive ones, so a run inside a dispatched child must not turn them into the child form. Verify: the same command then reports `15 passed (15)` and `VX tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n99: - [x] T016 Hold the renderer's child test equal to the spec gate's (`RCS`). Import `isChildSession` from `../../../system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs` and add one `it.each(['1', '0', 'true', ''])` case that stubs `AI_SESSION_CHILD` to the value, renders the start command the file's first case renders and expects `head.includes('(parent-named only)')` to equal `isChildSession({ AI_SESSION_CHILD: value })`. Add a comment saying the renderer keeps its own literal so the runtime build has no edge into the spec kit, and this case keeps the two rules equal. It passes today and fails the day one rule changes alone. Verify: `VX tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed with 4 more cases than before.\n100: - [x] T017 Render `(needs a mode)` whatever row the id has (`RD`, `GT`). Test first: in `GT`, add a separate `it` outside `HEAD_CASES`, because that table asserts no head prints a `command-` id. It renders `{ skill: 'command-create-agent', needsMode: true, confidence: 0.95, uncertainty: 0.12, passes_threshold: true }` and expects the head to hold `(needs a mode)` and not `/create:agent`. Then in `commandLabel` read the generated row only when `recommendation.needsMode !== true`, and remove the `commandRowFor(top.skill) === undefined` clause from `headLabel`, because the first edit alone drops the label. Verify: before the change the case fails with `/create:agent (start)`, after it `VX tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n101: - [x] T018 Take the child downgrade's class from the printed command's row (`RD`, `RCS`). Test first: in `RCS`, add a case that stubs `AI_SESSION_CHILD` to `1`, renders `{ skill: 'command-speckit-search', kind: 'command', command: '/doctor:speckit', policy: 'run' }` with the file's scores and expects the head to hold `/doctor:speckit (parent-named only)`. Then in `commandLabel`, pass `row.mutating` only when `row.command` equals the printed command, and otherwise the `mutating` of the first `COMMAND_ROWS` entry whose `command` equals it, importing `COMMAND_ROWS` beside `commandRowFor`. A command with no row passes `undefined`, which `parentNamedOnly` already treats as writing. Add a comment saying the class belongs to the command printed, not to the skill that carried it. Verify: before the change the case fails with `(run)`, after it `VX tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` report 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n102: \n103: ### Wave 1, lane WG4: behaviour runner containment\n104: - [x] T019 Let a test import the runner (`R`). Wrap the final `try` that awaits `main` in `if (invokedDirectly)`, with `invokedDirectly` defined as `S` defines it. Add `export` to `G2_ROWS` and `childEnv`. Add the comment `S` carries, saying the tables are exported for direct tests, so the CLI runs only when this file is the entry point. Verify: `node --check $R` exits 0, `node -e \"import('./$R').then((m) => console.log(Object.keys(m).sort().join(',')))\"` prints `G2_ROWS,childEnv` and nothing else, and `node $R --list g2 | head -1` prints `g2-deep-research-ask`.\n105: - [x] T020 Mark an arena the builder made (`ARB`). In `buildArena`, after `assertHead(dest, head)`, write the head and a newline to `join(dest, '.git', MARK)` with `writeFileSync`, and add a comment saying the runner refuses a live arm in a checkout without this file, because only a checkout built here has no remote, no outer repository and no dotenv file in its copied build trees. Verify: `node --check $ARB` exits 0 and `rg -c \"skilled-behaviour-arena\" $ARB` prints 1. T059 builds one arena.\n106: - [x] T021 Build the child environment from an allowlist (`R`, `BG`). Test first: create `BG` with a case that stubs `SSH_AUTH_SOCK`, `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `NPM_TOKEN`, `GH_TOKEN`, `AI_SESSION_CHILD` and `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, calls `childEnv('/tmp/gh-empty')` from `R` and expects the first five absent, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `PATH` and `HOME` present, `GH_CONFIG_DIR` equal to `/tmp/gh-empty`, `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT` equal to `0` and `GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0` equal to `credential.helper`. Then rebuild `childEnv` from `CHILD_ENV_NAMES` (`PATH`, `HOME`, `USER`, `LOGNAME`, `SHELL`, `TMPDIR`, `TMP`, `TEMP`, `LANG`, `TERM`, `TERM_PROGRAM`, `COLORTERM` and `NO_COLOR`) and `CHILD_ENV_PREFIXES` (`LC_`, `XDG_`, `ANTHROPIC_`, `CLAUDE_`, `CODEX_`, `OPENAI_`, `OPENCODE_`, `LLMGATEWAY_`, `PI_`, `DEVIN_`, `DSH_`, `DEEPSEEK_`, `OLLAMA_`, `SPECKIT_`, `SKILL_ADVISOR_`, `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_` and `MK_`), then set the GitHub and git overrides as today. Delete `GITHUB_TOKEN_VARS` and rewrite the comment above it to say a turn runs with bypassed permissions, so it gets only what a runtime needs to start and authenticate, and every other credential in the operator's shell stays out. Verify: before the change the case fails on `SSH_AUTH_SOCK`, after it `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node --check $R` exits 0.\n107: - [x] T022 Refuse a live arm outside a marked arena (`R`, `BG`). Test first: in `BG`, add a case on a temporary folder after `git init -q`: `liveArmRefusal(dir)` returns code `arena_unprepared`, after writing `<dir>/.git/MARK` it returns `null` and after `git remote add origin https://example.invalid/x.git` it returns code `remote_present` with `remotes` `['origin']`. Then export `liveArmRefusal(root)`: it runs `git -C <root> -c core.fsmonitor=false remote` and returns the `remote_present` refusal when a name is listed, else resolves the output of `git -C <root> rev-parse --git-path MARK` against `root` and returns `{ ok: false, code: 'arena_unprepared', marker: <that path> }` when the file is missing, else `null`. In `runTurn`'s first-turn block, call it on `REPO_ROOT` in place of the `remoteNames()` check, still only when the run is not a dry run. Remove `remoteNames` when nothing else calls it. Add a comment saying a remote is the one way a turn reaches outside, and the marker proves the checkout came from the arena builder. Verify: before the change the import is `undefined` and the case fails, after it `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node --check $R` exits 0.\n108: - [x] T023 Label